# Git: local-root vs Lovable main (HARD — never confuse)

## Mental model (read this first)

| Location | Remote | Branch | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `d:\montfortre` (this Cursor workspace) | `FerozArshad/montfortre` | **always `local-root`** | Clone/layout only: full app + `montfortre-com/` + HTTrack + docs. **Local work only.** |
| `d:\montfortre\montfortre-loveable` | `smontfort/monttfortre` | **`main` only** | **The only deploy target.** Powers the live site. App paths at **repo root** (`src/`, `public/`, `supabase/`, …). |

**`local-root` exists so we can clone the full tree — nothing else.** It is not a deploy branch. Shipping = copy **rewritten** app files into the Lovable clone and push **that** — never merge between the two repos.

## Folder names (this workspace)

| Folder | Role |
|---|---|
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/` | App you edit (was `ghl-react/`) |
| `montfortre-loveable/` | Lovable deploy clone (was `GHL_Montfort_lovable/`) |
| `montfortre-com/` | HTTrack / design / SEO research (was `reference/`) — never ship |

## One-sentence rule

Work on `local-root`. Push **only** to the Lovable repo's `main`. **Never push to any other remote.**

## The only push target

- **Push to:** `https://github.com/smontfort/monttfortre.git` → branch `main`, from `d:\montfortre\montfortre-loveable`.
- **Never push to:** `FerozArshad/montfortre` — not `main`, not `local-root`, not any branch. Committing locally on `local-root` is fine as a local checkpoint, but **do not `git push`** there.
- Do **not** create `D:\GHL_Montfort_main_pushN` worktrees anymore. That workflow targeted the old GHL remote and is retired.
- When the user says “push / commit”, they mean **the Lovable repo's `main`**.
- The local working tree layout (`montfortre-ghl-studio/` under `local-root`) will **always** differ from the Lovable layout (app at repo root). That difference is intentional and permanent.

## Path rewriting (local-root → Lovable)

Copy **only** new/updated files under `montfortre-ghl-studio/`, paths **rewritten to repo root** (no `montfortre-ghl-studio/` prefix):

| Local working tree (`local-root`) | Path in the Lovable repo |
|---|---|
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/src/...` | `src/...` |
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/public/...` | `public/...` |
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/index.html` | `index.html` |
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/supabase/migrations/...` | `supabase/migrations/...` |
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/supabase/functions/...` | `supabase/functions/...` |
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/package.json` | `package.json` (only if the app needed a package change) |
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/HANDOFF*.md` | `HANDOFF*.md` |
| `montfortre-ghl-studio/seo-audit/...` | `seo-audit/...` |

Database changes ship as **migrations in this repo** — that is how they reach the live database.

When listing files for the user, use **Lovable paths only** (e.g. `src/pages/Foo.tsx`), never `montfortre-ghl-studio/src/...`.

## Never push

- `montfortre-com/` (HTTrack, CDN captures, blog notes)
- `.cursor/` (including this rule file — local only)
- Anything that exists only on the local-root parent layout
- `montfortre-ghl-studio/package-lock.json` unless the user explicitly asks
- The `montfortre-ghl-studio/` folder prefix itself
- Temp audit dumps (`_tmp_*`, live HTML captures, scratch scripts, `supabase/.temp`)

## Required ship workflow

1. Implement on `local-root` under `montfortre-ghl-studio/`.
2. Optionally `git commit` on `local-root` as a local checkpoint. **Do not push it.**
3. In `d:\montfortre\montfortre-loveable`: `git pull --ff-only origin main` first — Lovable's own agent commits there too, so always pull before copying.
4. Copy **only** the new/updated rewritten app files into that clone.
5. Review `git status` to confirm no scratch files or `montfortre-ghl-studio/` prefixes slipped in.
6. `git commit` then `git push origin main` (never force).
